"""Battery input and switch, battery measurement, supply selection, 3.3 V buck and 20 V boost.

Power tree. Three sources can power the board, and each reaches the rails through one path:
- Battery (J1, 3S LiPo): VBAT feeds the 20 V boost U1, the fan driver (drivers sheet), the
  addressable LEDs (peripherals sheet) and input IN1 of the power mux U4.
- USB (U2 VBUS, +5V): input IN2 of U4.
- SWD probe (P1 pin 1, SWD_VDD): the ideal diode U5 onto 3V3.
U4 puts the higher of VBAT and +5V on VSYS, which only feeds the 3V3 buck IC7. 3V3 then has
two sources: IC7, and U5 when the probe's supply is above it. The buck's high-side body diode
(DS13554 Figure 19) lifts VSYS from 3V3 to about 2.6-2.9 V when the probe alone powers the board
(known and accepted, boards/main/layout/README.md Power), but VSYS carries nothing else besides C52/C53,
and U4 blocks it from VBAT and +5V; VBAT and +5V are never powered from 3V3. With USB or the probe alone, VBAT stays
at 0 V, so the boost, the motor bridges and the fan driver are off: the motors cannot run in
the debug modes.

Battery input and switch. J1 takes the 3S LiPo: pack + on VBAT, pack - on GND_BAT. Q6
(HSBB3072, 30 V N-MOSFET) is a low-side switch from GND_BAT to the board GND, its gate pulled
to GND_BAT by R41 (100 kOhm); the slide switch SW4 drives it from VBAT through R43 (100 kOhm),
so VGS settles at VBAT / 2 (4.95-6.3 V; RDS(on) 3.8 mOhm max at 4.5 V, HSBB3072 p2) and stays
within the +-20 V rating. C58 (47 nF, gate to drain) sets the turn-on slew: on the Miller
plateau the drain moves at IG / CGD <= VBAT / (R43 x (C58 + Crss)) = 12.6 V / (100 kOhm x
47.2 nF) = 2.7 V/ms (Crss 229 pF, HSBB3072 p2), below the STSPIN958's 0.5 V/us dVS/dt rating
(DS14341 Table 1) on VBAT, and the inrush into the VBAT capacitors is about 2.7 V/ms x 288 uF
= 0.8 A. The body diode points from GND_BAT to GND, so the switch blocks battery current when
off.

Battery measurement: R44 100 kOhm / R45 27 kOhm from VBAT to GND into Battery_Voltage (PA5,
ADC12_INP19, DS13311 Table 8), C59 100 nF at the pin: 12.6 V x 27 / 127 = 2.68 V, below VDDA;
Thevenin 21.3 kOhm with 100 nF (2.1 ms) holds the pin for the ADC sample (CADC 4 pF, DS13311
Table 84) and filters the motor ripple. The firmware divides by 127 / 27 = 4.704.

Power mux, U4 (TPS2121RUXR, SLVSEA3F): IN1 on VBAT, IN2 on +5V, OUT on VSYS. PR1 and CP2 on
GND select VCOMP mode, the higher input powers the output (section 9.3.8, Table 9-3): the
battery whenever it is switched on, USB otherwise, with seamless switchover. OV1/OV2 on GND
(no overvoltage cut-off) and ST on GND (not read), as the pin table allows. Each channel is a
back-to-back FET pair with opposed body diodes (Figure 9-2), on only for the selected valid
input, so VSYS reaches neither input: the selected channel blocks a back-driven output (reverse
current blocking, section 9.3.6), and with no input above UVLO (2.4-2.8 V, Table 7.5) the output
is Hi-Z (Table 9-3), an off channel leaking at most 1 uA at 25 C, 5 uA to 85 C (Table 7.5,
ILK). R46 39 kOhm sets the current limit, Eq. 2: ILM = 65.2 / 39^0.861 = 2.8 A typ; Table 7.5
gives 2-3 A at 44.2 kOhm and 3-4 A at 29.8 kOhm, so at least 2 A, above the 1.3 A the buck
draws at 1.5 A out from 4.4 V. C61 100 nF on SS: 780-800 V/s output slew
(Table 9-1). Bypass at the pins (section 11): C62 1 uF on IN1, C63 10 uF on IN2 (the VBUS
bulk, at the 10 uF a USB device may put on VBUS, USB 2.0 section 7.2.4.1), C52/C53 on OUT.

3V3 buck, IC7 (L6981C33DR, fixed 3.3 V, low-consumption mode, DS13554). VIN and EN on VSYS.
In LCM the converter skips pulses at light load and turns its low side off at zero inductor
current (section 6.4.1, p10-11), and stops switching while FB is above its LCM threshold, 1.8 %
over the set point; it sinks current only in output overvoltage (section 6.6.1), so it does not
fight the probe's supply on 3V3. The datasheet does not cover VIN below its 3.5 V minimum with
the output held up, the probe-only state (README Open items: a bench check). Integrator parts per DS13554
Table 1 p3 and Table 2 p4:
- C55 100 nF BOOT to SW (100 nF typ);
- C54 1 uF on VCC (>= 1 uF);
- L3 22 uH (YSPIA0645-220M, 4.5 A Isat). Ripple by Eq. 36: 0.26-0.28 A for VIN 11.1-12.6 V,
  18 % of the 1.5 A rating, below the 20-40 % target of section 8.4.2 p27 (a target, not a
  limit: the Eq. 39 peak, 1.64 A, stays under the 2.0 A minimum current limit);
- input: C52 10 uF + C53 1 uF on VSYS next to IC7 (CIN 10 uF typ, Table 2);
- output: C56 and C57 22 uF on 3V3. With every capacitor on 3V3 the rail carries 71.8 uF
  nominal, inside the 30.5-145 uF that Eq. 42/43 allow the internal compensation at 3.3 V.

20 V boost, U1 (TPS61178RNWR, auto PFM, SLVSDA7E). VIN on VBAT, VOUT on +20V for the L6205
bridges, EN on Motors_Enable (PA10): the boost runs only while the firmware enables the
motors, and its internal 800 kOhm pull-down (REN, section 7.5 p6) with R49 on the drivers
sheet hold it off in reset. In PFM it skips cycles at light load (section 8.4.2) instead of
switching at full frequency. Integrator parts:
- R36 140 kOhm FREQ/SYNC to GND: Eq. 2-3 p13-14, 1 / (3 x 1.8 pF x 140 kOhm + 50 ns) =
  1.24 MHz;
- R37 56 kOhm ILIMIT to GND: Eq. 1 p12, 745 / 56 = 13.3 A typ;
- R39 1 MOhm / R40 68 kOhm FB divider: Eq. 4 p17, VOUT = 1.198 V x (1 + 1000 / 68) =
  18.82 V typ, 18.19-19.42 V over VREF (1.180-1.210 V, section 7.5), 1 % resistors and the
  60 nA FB leakage through R39: below the 20 V maximum output (section 7.3) and the 20.5 V
  overvoltage threshold, with RDOWN below 100 kOhm (section 9.2.4 p18);
- L2 1 uH (XAL6030-102, 23 A Isat): ripple by Eq. 5, VIN x (1 - VIN / VOUT) / (L x fSW),
  3.78 A p-p at 9.9 V and less at higher VIN, below the 4 A of section 9.2.4.1 p19;
- R38 68 kOhm + C42 470 pF COMP network (section 9.2.4.4 p21-24; CP omitted, which p24
  allows below 10 pF);
- C43 220 nF BST to SW (0.1-1 uF, >= 10 V: section 8.3.12 p14);
- C48 4.7 uF on VCC (> 1 uF, pin table p3);
- input C49-C51 3 x 22 uF on VBAT (section 9.2.4.3 p21), output C44/C45 10 uF 50 V and
  C46/C47 22 uF 35 V on +20V (section 9.2.4.2 p21);
- DISDRV unconnected: there is no output-disconnect FET (pin table p3). With EN low, +20V
  follows VBAT through the high-side body diode, and the bridges stay disabled by the same
  Motors_Enable.

SWD probe supply, U5 (LM66100DCKR ideal diode, SLVSEZ8A): VIN on SWD_VDD (P1 pin 1), VOUT on
3V3, CE on VOUT for always-on reverse current blocking (section 8.3.2): the probe powers 3V3
only while its supply is above 3V3, and the board never drives the probe's supply. ST on GND
(pin table p3). C64 1 uF on VIN (section 10).
"""

load(
    "./passives.zen",
    "C_100N_0402",
    "C_10U_0603",
    "C_1U_0402",
    "C_220N_0603",
    "C_22U_0805_25V",
    "C_22U_0805_35V",
    "C_470P_0402",
    "C_47N_0603",
    "C_4U7_0805",
    "C_10U_0805",
    "R_100K_0402",
    "R_140K_0402",
    "R_1M_0603",
    "R_27K_0402",
    "R_39K_0402",
    "R_56K_0402",
    "R_68K_0402",
    "R_68K_0603",
)

Capacitor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Capacitor.zen")
Resistor = Module("@stdlib/generics/Resistor.zen")
B02B_PASK = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/jst/B02B-PASK/B02B-PASK.zen")
HSBB3072 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/huashuo/HSBB3072/HSBB3072.zen")
L6981 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/st/L6981/L6981.zen")
LM66100 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/ti/LM66100/LM66100.zen")
MK_12D18_G040 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/g-switch/MK-12D18-G040/MK-12D18-G040.zen")
TPS2121 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/ti/TPS2121/TPS2121.zen")
TPS61178 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/ti/TPS61178/TPS61178.zen")
XAL6030_102 = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/coilcraft/XAL6030-102/XAL6030-102.zen")
YSPIA0645_220M = Module("github.com/Team-Micras/MicrasPCB/components/yjycoin/YSPIA0645-220M/YSPIA0645-220M.zen")

VBAT = io(Power)
V3V3 = io(Power)
V5V = io(Power)
V20V = io(Power)
SWD_VDD = io(Power)
GND = io(Ground)
GND_BAT = io(Net)
MOTORS_ENABLE = io(Net)
BATTERY_VOLTAGE = io(Net)

# The buck's input: VBAT or +5V through U4, whichever is higher (USB 4.4-5.25 V, battery up to
# 12.6 V); the RCB release keeps it within 50 mV of the input in use (SLVSEA3F Table 7.5).
VSYS = Power("VSYS", voltage="4.4V to 12.6V")
BAT_SW_DRIVE = Net("BAT_SW_DRIVE")
BAT_SW_GATE = Net("BAT_SW_GATE")
MUX_ILM = Net("MUX_ILM")
MUX_SS = Net("MUX_SS")
BUCK_SW = Net("BUCK_SW")
BUCK_BOOT = Net("BUCK_BOOT")
# The L6981 VCC LDO output, 3.3 V typ (DS13554 Table 6 p7).
BUCK_VCC = Power("BUCK_VCC", voltage="3.0V to 3.6V")
BOOST_SW = Net("BOOST_SW")
BOOST_BST = Net("BOOST_BST")
# The TPS61178 VCC LDO output, 6 V typ (SLVSDA7E section 7.5 p5).
BOOST_VCC = Power("BOOST_VCC", voltage="6V")
BOOST_FREQ = Net("BOOST_FREQ")
BOOST_ILIM = Net("BOOST_ILIM")
BOOST_FB = Net("BOOST_FB")
BOOST_COMP = Net("BOOST_COMP")
BOOST_COMP_RC = Net("BOOST_COMP_RC")

# Battery input and switch.
B02B_PASK(name="J1", prefix="J", P1=VBAT, P2=GND_BAT)
MK_12D18_G040(name="SW4", A=NotConnected(), COM=VBAT, B=BAT_SW_DRIVE)
Resistor(name="R43", P1=BAT_SW_DRIVE, P2=BAT_SW_GATE, **R_100K_0402)
HSBB3072(name="Q6", G=BAT_SW_GATE, S=GND_BAT, D=GND)
Resistor(name="R41", P1=GND_BAT, P2=BAT_SW_GATE, **R_100K_0402)
Capacitor(name="C58", P1=GND, P2=BAT_SW_GATE, **C_47N_0603)

# Battery measurement.
Resistor(name="R44", P1=VBAT, P2=BATTERY_VOLTAGE, **R_100K_0402)
Resistor(name="R45", P1=GND, P2=BATTERY_VOLTAGE, **R_27K_0402)
Capacitor(name="C59", P1=GND, P2=BATTERY_VOLTAGE, **C_100N_0402)

# Supply selection.
TPS2121(
    name="U4",
    IN1=VBAT,
    IN2=V5V,
    OUT=VSYS,
    GND=GND,
    PR1=GND,
    CP2=GND,
    OV1=GND,
    OV2=GND,
    ST=GND,
    ILM=MUX_ILM,
    SS=MUX_SS,
)
Resistor(name="R46", P1=GND, P2=MUX_ILM, **R_39K_0402)
Capacitor(name="C61", P1=GND, P2=MUX_SS, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C62", P1=GND, P2=VBAT, **C_1U_0402)
Capacitor(name="C63", P1=GND, P2=V5V, **C_10U_0603)

# 3V3 buck.
L6981(
    name="IC7",
    mpn="L6981C33DR",
    VIN=VSYS,
    EN=VSYS,
    VOUT=V3V3,
    VCC=BUCK_VCC,
    GND=GND,
    SW=BUCK_SW,
    BOOT=BUCK_BOOT,
)
Capacitor(name="C55", P1=BUCK_BOOT, P2=BUCK_SW, **C_100N_0402)
Capacitor(name="C54", P1=GND, P2=BUCK_VCC, **C_1U_0402)
YSPIA0645_220M(name="L3", P1=BUCK_SW, P2=V3V3)
Capacitor(name="C52", P1=GND, P2=VSYS, **C_10U_0603)
Capacitor(name="C53", P1=GND, P2=VSYS, **C_1U_0402)
Capacitor(name="C56", P1=GND, P2=V3V3, **C_22U_0805_25V)
Capacitor(name="C57", P1=GND, P2=V3V3, **C_22U_0805_25V)

# SWD probe supply.
LM66100(name="U5", VIN=SWD_VDD, VOUT=V3V3, CE=V3V3, ST=GND, GND=GND)
Capacitor(name="C64", P1=GND, P2=SWD_VDD, **C_1U_0402)

# 20 V boost.
TPS61178(
    name="U1",
    mpn="TPS61178RNWR",
    VIN=VBAT,
    EN=MOTORS_ENABLE,
    VOUT=V20V,
    VCC=BOOST_VCC,
    GND=GND,
    SW=BOOST_SW,
    BST=BOOST_BST,
    FB=BOOST_FB,
    COMP=BOOST_COMP,
    FREQ=BOOST_FREQ,
    ILIMIT=BOOST_ILIM,
    DISDRV=NotConnected(),
)
Resistor(name="R36", P1=GND, P2=BOOST_FREQ, **R_140K_0402)
Resistor(name="R37", P1=GND, P2=BOOST_ILIM, **R_56K_0402)
Resistor(name="R39", P1=BOOST_FB, P2=V20V, **R_1M_0603)
Resistor(name="R40", P1=GND, P2=BOOST_FB, **R_68K_0603)
Resistor(name="R38", P1=BOOST_COMP_RC, P2=BOOST_COMP, **R_68K_0402)
Capacitor(name="C42", P1=GND, P2=BOOST_COMP_RC, **C_470P_0402)
Capacitor(name="C43", P1=BOOST_SW, P2=BOOST_BST, **C_220N_0603)
Capacitor(name="C48", P1=GND, P2=BOOST_VCC, **C_4U7_0805)
XAL6030_102(name="L2", P1=BOOST_SW, P2=VBAT)
Capacitor(name="C49", P1=GND, P2=VBAT, **C_22U_0805_25V)
Capacitor(name="C50", P1=GND, P2=VBAT, **C_22U_0805_25V)
Capacitor(name="C51", P1=GND, P2=VBAT, **C_22U_0805_25V)
Capacitor(name="C44", P1=GND, P2=V20V, **C_10U_0805)
Capacitor(name="C45", P1=GND, P2=V20V, **C_10U_0805)
Capacitor(name="C46", P1=GND, P2=V20V, **C_22U_0805_35V)
Capacitor(name="C47", P1=GND, P2=V20V, **C_22U_0805_35V)
